---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
import { CONSENT_LINE } from '@data/check-quiz';
import { themeConfig } from '~/theme.config';
import { SPONSORS_ENABLED } from '@data/site';

const title = 'Privacy';
const description = SPONSORS_ENABLED
  ? `How ${themeConfig.name} handles the self-check, optional email, lesson progress on your device, and partner links.`
  : `How ${themeConfig.name} handles the self-check, optional email, and lesson progress on your device.`;
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} robots="noindex, follow">
  <p class="course-kicker">Privacy</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">What this site keeps</h1>
  <div class="lesson-prose page-prose">
    <p>This site does not ask you to create an account. There are no advertising pixels.</p>
    <h2>The self-check</h2>
    <p>
      The only form that can send answers to us is the free check at <a href="/check">/check</a>. Before you submit, the page says: “{CONSENT_LINE}”
    </p>
    <p>The questions run in your browser. If you leave before the last step, nothing is sent. The course is for everyone. If the age range is under 18, we do not ask for an email, we do not store an email, and we store the check answers anonymously only. The plan still shows on the page.</p>
    <p>If you finish and the save works, we store the answers you picked from the lists:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Age range</li>
      <li>Country or region, from a short list, not a street address</li>
      <li>Main struggle, how long, how often, and the main trigger</li>
      <li>Faith background, only if you answer that question</li>
      <li>What you want most from the next 30 days</li>
      <li>How you heard about the site</li>
      <li>Which plan variant and track the check recommended</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not store your name, IP address, or browser. The rows sit in a Cloudflare D1 database on the free tier, through a Pages Function. There is no secret and no third-party analytics key in this project.</p>
    <p>If saving fails, days 1 to 7 still appear on the page and nothing from that attempt is stored.</p>
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>The email field is optional for anyone 18 or older. Leave it blank and we store no email, and we do not send one. If the age range is under 18, that field is not shown, and an email in the request is not stored.</p>
    <p>
      If you enter an email on the check, we store that address with the answers and try to send the 30-day plan from plan@calltoreset.site. If you enter an email on a later phase, we store that address on its own and send the same plan. Days 1 to 7 stay on the page if sending fails. The rest of the plan does not. To remove an address, the person who operates the site deletes that row. There is no
      account page for it yet.
    </p>
    <h2>Newsletter</h2>
    <p>The join form asks for an email only. If you send it, we store that address in the same Cloudflare D1 database and add you as a contact in Plunk, marked subscribed. This form does not send the plan. To come off the list, the person who operates the site deletes that row and the Plunk contact. There is no account page for it yet.</p>
    <h2>30-day reset list</h2>
    <p>The 30-day reset list form asks for an email and, if you want, a first name. If you send it, we store the email, the name, the page you signed up on and the date in Cloudflare KV on the free tier, through a Pages Function. We do not store your IP address or browser, and the form sends no email and calls no other service. To come off the list, ask and the person who operates the site deletes your entry.</p>
    <h2>Share buttons</h2>
    <p>The share buttons are plain links to X, Facebook and WhatsApp, or your device's own share sheet. Nothing loads from those sites until you click one.</p>
    <h2>On your device</h2>
    <p>When you mark a lesson done, the browser stores that mark in localStorage on your device. Clearing site data removes it. We do not receive that list.</p>
    {SPONSORS_ENABLED ? (
      <>
        <h2>Partners</h2>
        <p>Partner cards link away from the site, or to the partner page. Those links include utm_medium=sponsor and utm_content set to the placement, so a partner can tell which slot was clicked. We do not add your name or email to those links.</p>
      </>
    ) : null}
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>Pages are static files. A host such as Cloudflare may log ordinary web requests. We do not copy those logs into the check database. We do not sell this information.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
